  "category": "Computational linguistics",
  "type": "person",
  "definition": "Johann-Mattis List (born 16 July 1981 in Kassel, Germany) is a German scientist.",
  "details": "He is known for his work on quantitative comparative linguistics. List is currently professor at the University of Passau, Germany, where he leads the Chair of Multilingual Computational Linguistics.",
  "explainer": {
    "lead": "Johann-Mattis List is a German scientist. His work spans digital humanities.",
    "contributions": [
      {
        "name": "He has also co-authored various papers on computational language phylogeny, including on the Sino-Tibetan languages, and has introduced the concept of incomplete lineage sorting in historical linguistics.",
